use "@std"

Note: Phase 26 migration smoke test - pre-migration form
Note: Exercises every walker path before the Wave 3 mass sweep.

Note: Basic infix arithmetic
Int a = (add 1 2)
Int b = (sub 5 3)
Int c = (mul 4 2)
Note: (div Int Int) auto-promotes to Double per D-08 - declare Double targets
Double d = (div 10 5)

Note: Precedence - Star/Slash binds tighter than Plus/Minus
Int e = (add 1 (mul 2 3))
Double f = (sub 10 (div 4 2))

Note: Parenthesised - outer parens preserved, inner-rewrite recurses
Int g = (mul ((add 1 2)) 3)

Note: Unary minus on identifier - parser shorthand to (neg IDENT)
Int x = 5
Int y = (neg x)

Note: Identifier-on-identifier infix
Int p = 10
Int q = 20
Int r = (add p q)

Note: Mixed Float/Double via existing widening (already prefix-friendly)
Double pi = 3.14
Double tau = (mul pi 2.0)

Note: Note-stream - Plus/Minus inside | ... | MUST be pass-through (Pitfall 3)
Note: Cent offset (+50c) is a known-good note-stream typed literal that round-trips
Sequence s = | C4q D4q E4+50c F4q |

(print (str a))
(print (str e))
(print (str g))
(print (str y))
(print (str r))
(print (str tau))
